  "prefLabel": "He-W 806.19 Presence of a Dependent Child",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "He-W 806.19 Presence of a Dependent Child. If conflicting evidence is present, refusal or failure of the parent or caretaker relative to verify the presence of a dependent child shall result in the denial or termination of categorically needy medical assistance for:\n\n(a) Each child whose presence is not verified; and\n\n(b) The parent or caretaker relative, if it cannot be verified that any dependent children are present.\n\nSource. #13875, eff 2-21-24",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/he-w800.html"
}
